# B"H
<!-- Boruch Hashem -->
<!-- Blessed is He -->

# Final Execution Plan

> The Awtsmoos permits one measured trial while the deployed meadow remains untouched;
> Awtsmoos.com records every candidate receipt before any future source may be adjusted.

## Read-Only Actions

1. Capture `git diff --stat`, exact changed paths, timestamps, and hashes.
2. Verify the local compact artifact contains the deferred scheduler boundary expected by the native boot contract.
3. Run:
	- route-shell tests;
	- native boot contract;
	- readiness settlement tests;
	- feature scheduler tests;
	- CompactJS real-runtime test;
	- any bootstrap-minimap tests found in the repository.
4. Launch the current working tree through `BrowserProofProcess.mjs` and a fresh isolated CDP target.
5. Record:
	- time to diagnostics publication;
	- time to essential receipt;
	- time to playable;
	- six-system readiness;
	- minimap count and bootstrap ownership;
	- console exceptions;
	- failed requests;
	- movement distance.
6. Run `OptionalMultiplayerSurfaceDiagnostic.mjs` against two local pages and preserve its snapshots.
7. Compare candidate bytes, timing, requests, and errors with production release `d77341824`.
8. Write an audit verdict: green candidate, candidate with blockers, or rejected candidate.

## Forbidden Actions

- No source rewrite.
- No compact regeneration.
- No staging.
- No commit.
- No push.
- No deployment.
- No deletion or reset of local changes.
- No contact with Android-emulator files.

## Promotion Gate

A later source or deployment phase may begin only after every read-only gate is green and the candidate demonstrably improves or preserves production startup, gameplay, network, minimap, chat, and movement behavior.
